# [DD-13b.W23.3] S-R2's ACCEPT half. A `provenance` record whose fidelity
# is `verbatim` owes no `adaptation` line, and this file is what says so
# — the pair's refusing half (`prov_adapted_no_adaptation.rxtin`) is
# satisfiable by a parser that simply refuses every `provenance` record,
# which is why the accept control is not optional.
#
# WHY THE PAIR LIVES HERE AND NOT IN THE BENCH (r57 S-M3): the bench's
# own acceptance checks C5/C6 test this same rule in the OTHER repo, and
# a sabotage row planted into pcrec whose only detector is in pcrec-bench
# would score UNDETECTED in `make mech` and be RIGHT to — a row's
# detector must live in this repo's matrix.
pattern a+
provenance
  source authored
  retrieved 2026-09-15
  license MIT
  fidelity verbatim
m "aaa" 0 3
